1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,758
Since you started

2
00:00:00,778 --> 00:00:02,302
scrolling, your heart has

3
00:00:02,322 --> 00:00:04,186
beaten hundreds of times…

4
00:00:04,377 --> 00:00:05,042
and you never

5
00:00:05,062 --> 00:00:06,322
told it to once.

6
00:00:06,397 --> 00:00:07,190
And it's never

7
00:00:07,210 --> 00:00:08,226
waited for you.

8
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:09,163
So who's been

9
00:00:09,183 --> 00:00:10,281
running the show?

10
00:00:10,635 --> 00:00:11,602
Tucked in the heart's

11
00:00:11,622 --> 00:00:13,006
upper right chamber is

12
00:00:13,026 --> 00:00:14,422
a tiny patch of cells

13
00:00:14,442 --> 00:00:16,237
called the SA node.

14
00:00:16,428 --> 00:00:16,814
It's your

15
00:00:16,834 --> 00:00:18,149
built-in pacemaker.

16
00:00:18,169 --> 00:00:19,345
It fires its own

17
00:00:19,365 --> 00:00:20,683
electrical spark,

18
00:00:20,712 --> 00:00:23,272
about 100,000 times a day.

19
00:00:23,347 --> 00:00:24,967
It never asked you once.

20
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:25,835
Heart cells

21
00:00:25,855 --> 00:00:27,089
grown in a dish,

22
00:00:27,109 --> 00:00:29,190
with no body and no brain,

23
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:30,865
start beating on their own.

24
00:00:31,056 --> 00:00:31,547
So what does

25
00:00:31,567 --> 00:00:32,607
your brain do?

26
00:00:32,868 --> 00:00:33,718
You know that jolt

27
00:00:33,738 --> 00:00:34,987
from a jump scare,

28
00:00:35,015 --> 00:00:36,296
when your heart races

29
00:00:36,316 --> 00:00:37,715
before you even think?

30
00:00:38,162 --> 00:00:38,978
That's your brain

31
00:00:38,998 --> 00:00:40,409
cranking the volume up.

32
00:00:40,542 --> 00:00:41,300
Falling asleep,

33
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:42,452
it turns it down.

34
00:00:42,585 --> 00:00:43,714
Try it now:

35
00:00:43,734 --> 00:00:45,235
breathe in slowly and your

36
00:00:45,255 --> 00:00:46,829
pulse speeds up slightly.

37
00:00:46,904 --> 00:00:48,733
Breathe out, it slows.

38
00:00:48,924 --> 00:00:50,091
Here's the twist:

39
00:00:50,352 --> 00:00:51,156
most of the time,

40
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:51,737
your brain is

41
00:00:51,757 --> 00:00:52,913
pressing the brake.

42
00:00:53,104 --> 00:00:54,396
In a heart transplant,

43
00:00:54,416 --> 00:00:55,722
the nerves are cut.

44
00:00:55,797 --> 00:00:57,533
The new heart still beats…

45
00:00:57,724 --> 00:00:58,845
just faster.

46
00:00:59,036 --> 00:01:00,422
It even has backups,

47
00:01:00,442 --> 00:01:01,072
like your phone's

48
00:01:01,092 --> 00:01:02,201
low-power mode.

49
00:01:02,276 --> 00:01:03,661
If the main spark fails,

50
00:01:03,681 --> 00:01:04,369
a second spot

51
00:01:04,389 --> 00:01:06,183
takes over, slower.

52
00:01:06,258 --> 00:01:07,086
If that fails,

53
00:01:07,106 --> 00:01:08,702
a third, slower still.

54
00:01:08,836 --> 00:01:09,651
And when backups

55
00:01:09,671 --> 00:01:10,487
aren't enough,

56
00:01:10,507 --> 00:01:12,197
doctors fit a pacemaker.

57
00:01:12,272 --> 00:01:13,309
That small bump some

58
00:01:13,329 --> 00:01:14,110
grandparents have

59
00:01:14,130 --> 00:01:15,320
under the collarbone?

60
00:01:15,581 --> 00:01:16,470
That's it,

61
00:01:16,545 --> 00:01:18,675
doing the SA node's job.

62
00:01:18,751 --> 00:01:19,790
The one catch:

63
00:01:20,144 --> 00:01:21,250
your heart still needs

64
00:01:21,270 --> 00:01:22,910
oxygen, and breathing

65
00:01:22,930 --> 00:01:24,306
is your brain's job.

66
00:01:24,497 --> 00:01:25,583
But the beat?

67
00:01:25,612 --> 00:01:26,091
It's doing

68
00:01:26,111 --> 00:01:27,252
that right now.

69
00:01:27,272 --> 00:01:28,405
Without asking.

70
00:01:28,596 --> 00:01:29,551
Follow for more

71
00:01:29,571 --> 00:01:30,747
things your body does

72
00:01:30,767 --> 00:01:32,433
without asking you.

